# igs-pharma.be staging env (asafarim-platform#822, roadmap IGS-D5). PLACEHOLDERS ONLY.
# The real file is infra/igs/.env.igs.age (age-encrypted to .age/key.pub). To edit on the VPS:
#   age -d -i .age/key.txt infra/igs/.env.igs.age > infra/igs/.env.igs
#   $EDITOR infra/igs/.env.igs
#   age -R .age/key.pub -o infra/igs/.env.igs.age infra/igs/.env.igs
# igs-deploy.sh refuses to deploy while any value below still contains CHANGE_ME.
# Separate from every other app's env: nothing here is shared with asafarim-com.

# --- Deploy-only (IGS_*): read by the compose file and igs-deploy.sh, NEVER passed to an app ---
# Password of the dedicated igs-postgres superuser `igs` (URL-safe, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
IGS_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
# DDL-capable connection for igs-migrate and the operator CLIs only (the owner `igs`).
IGS_MIGRATOR_DATABASE_URL=postgres://igs:CHANGE_ME@igs-postgres:5432/igs
# The runtime logins (#841), created by infra/scripts/igs-db-roles.sh; each password set
# once with `\password` (see that script). Host igs-postgres: the database certificate's name.
# igs-web and igs-platform:
IGS_APP_DATABASE_URL=postgres://igs_app_login:CHANGE_ME@igs-postgres:5432/igs
# igs-worker (and igs-migrate's runtime DATABASE_URL, which it never uses):
IGS_WORKER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://igs_worker_login:CHANGE_ME@igs-postgres:5432/igs
# Optional IP filter in front of platform.igs-pharma.be. Empty or unset (the default): the
# back-office is open to every network and its staff sign-in protects it (passkey + 2-step
# login, staff-only sessions, per-IP rate limits); igs-deploy.sh then refuses an igs-pharma
# image older than that hardening (d4a1eb8). Set it to turn the filter back on, no code change:
# IPv4/IPv6 CIDRs with a prefix, comma- or space-separated, e.g. "203.0.113.7/32, 2001:db8:1234::/64";
# everyone else then gets a 403. Rendered into the edge site file on the server only.
IGS_PLATFORM_ALLOW_IPS=
# Optional: a Discord webhook URL (https://discord.com/api/webhooks/...) for the health
# check's alerts (igs-healthcheck.timer). Left as CHANGE_ME, the check only logs.
IGS_ALERT_WEBHOOK_DISCORD=CHANGE_ME
# Nightly encrypted backups (igs-backup.timer, #829). All six set, or no backups (the
# deploy warns). Any S3-compatible store, path-style addressing:
# e.g. https://fra1.digitaloceanspaces.com + fra1, or https://leafcloud.store + europe-nl-ams.
IGS_BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=CHANGE_ME
IGS_BACKUP_S3_REGION=CHANGE_ME
IGS_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=CHANGE_ME
# A key limited to that bucket.
IGS_BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY=CHANGE_ME
IGS_BACKUP_S3_SECRET_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# The age PUBLIC key (age1...) backups are encrypted to. The private key stays offline.
IGS_BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT=CHANGE_ME

# --- App runtime (igs-web, igs-platform, igs-worker) ---
# No DATABASE_URL here: the compose file sets each service's from the IGS_*_DATABASE_URL
# above (#841), and igs-deploy.sh leaves one out of the apps' env file.
AUTH_SECRET=CHANGE_ME
# >= 32 characters (audit-log.md).
AUDIT_HMAC_KEY=CHANGE_ME
ENCRYPTION_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# Storefront gate: coming-soon (closed, noindex) until Gate 1. igs-web defaults to it.
SITE_GATE=coming-soon
# AUTH_URL is set per app in infra/igs/docker-compose.yml (https://igs-pharma.be and
# https://platform.igs-pharma.be): one env file serves both apps.
